   "verdict": "partial",
   "gap": "Durrett's notation for special cases (pp. 23-24) is not set out: the integral of f(x) dx for Lebesgue measure on R^d, the integral from a to b of f(x) dx for E = [a, b], the integral of f(x) dG(x) for the Stieltjes measure of G, and a sum of f(i) over i for counting measure. The integration chapter states none of these conventions; the route later writes dx and integrals from a to b without stating them (the dG and counting-measure readings appear only in def:p15-convolution-law and the product-measures annex).",
